Modifications made in Vcode:
 - Renamed the application to Vcode and changed the application id to com.vcode.studio
 - Renamed the Kotlin/Java packages from com.blacksquircle to com.vcode and renamed
   identifiers that carried the original product name
 - New launcher icon and splash screen
 - Added syntax highlighting for Swift, R, PowerShell, Objective-C, Less, SCSS,
   CoffeeScript, Pug, Diff and Handlebars
 - Added keyword suggestions for code completion
 - Added a GitHub Actions workflow that builds and publishes the FOSS APK
 - Pinned bouncycastle and jsch to older versions to keep the build working
 - Removed the Google Play services flavor and its in-app update dependency
 - Release builds work without a signing key and leave dependency and VCS metadata out of the APK
 - Added a command palette, a status bar, breadcrumbs, a Kotlin plugin API, browsing and editing of archives, DEX files and compiled XML, and a library viewer with an ARM64 disassembler written in Rust

Third-party software added by Vcode: smali, baksmali and dexlib2 (Google's fork, BSD 3-clause license),
yaxpeax-arm (0BSD license), ghidra-decompiler (Apache-2.0 license, a Rust port of the Ghidra decompiler), object, cpp_demangle and rustc-demangle (Apache-2.0 or MIT license) and jni (MIT or Apache-2.0 license).

